{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nImplement the contract decided by the preceding architecture story without changing the production write route yet. The key deliverable is sufficient deterministic parity evidence to make the later cutover/deletion safe within this epic.\n\nExisting useful assets include the real store-copy scrub/isolation fixtures, canonical serialization, route census, verified Cloud/DC fakes, and comprehensive mutation tests. Reuse them rather than creating a parallel reconciler harness.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Introduce the approved direction/action payload union and thread it through planner and coordinator boundaries up to a side-effect-free adapter projection seam.\n- Build a versioned corpus from deterministic synthetic tickets plus a scrubbed representative store snapshot. Include edge and failure shapes, not credentials or live bindings.\n- Drive legacy and typed planning/serialization over identical observations. Capture canonical normalized intent/outcome traces without invoking either writer.\n- Compare ordering, fields, identity scopes, diagnostics, follow-ons, suppression, retry dispositions, and modeled final state.\n- Run this oracle in default portable CI with no Jira, Docker, external service, or CI-provider dependency.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` — typed payloads and the effect-free trace projection.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` — portable replay and verified adapter contracts.\n- `tests/fixtures/` — versioned synthetic/scrubbed corpus with no credentials or live bindings.\n\n## Testing\n\nHappy path: representative inbound and outbound mutations produce matching normalized legacy/typed traces and modeled state. Edge/failure paths: malformed payloads, ambiguous commits, exhaustion, suppression, follow-ons, and cross-project routes either match or produce an approved named delta. Effect spies fail if the shadow path reaches Jira, the ticket store, a subprocess, clock sleep, or network.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Planners and coordinator use named payload types for every supported direction/action pair; construction rejects missing, extra critical, or wrong-action fields before effects.\n- [ ] The shadow comparator executes no Jira transport or ticket-store write, proven with failing spies on every effect seam.\n- [ ] The corpus covers create/update/delete/probe/conflict, inbound-only actions, links/comments/labels/status/parent/assignee/binding fields, duplicate and malformed inputs, suppression/follow-ons, ambiguous outcomes, retry exhaustion, and multi-project routing.\n- [ ] Replaying the same corpus is deterministic and idempotent; corpus version/provenance and normalization rules are explicit.\n- [ ] Legacy and typed traces have zero unexplained differences. Each intentional delta has a named test, rationale, and approval recorded on the ticket.\n- [ ] Verified-fake Jira Cloud and Data Center adapter contract tests pass without selecting a live backend.\n- [ ] Production continues to use the pre-cutover route in this story: the story's diff touches no production dispatch entry point (`typed_dispatch._LEAVES`, `batch_dispatch._mutation_to_batch_dict`, `applier.apply()`, or any producer in `differ.py` / `outbound_mutation_builders.py` / `run_differs.py` / `outbound_pass.py` / `binding_walk.py` / `invariants.py`) — verified by an explicit route-census check (a test asserting each of those callables is byte-identical / import-reachable and unmodified in this change) — and no module introduced by this story is later relied upon as a permanent production write path (verified by: every new module lives under the shadow-only seam named in Scope, is exercised only by tests, and is not imported by any of the production entry points just named)."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788108343209051286,"uuid":"d41e8c4d-3af7-442c-af1b-a0cb17c7da2b"}